meta {
  name: 11 Get Emergency Pricing Status
  type: http
  seq: 11
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/registration-settings/emergency-pricing
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

tests {
  test("200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });
  test("returns the resolved emergency-pricing state", function () {
    const d = res.getBody().data;
    expect(d).to.have.property("active");
    expect(d).to.have.property("reason");
    expect(d).to.have.property("applyInNonOperatingHours");
    expect(d).to.have.property("overrideEmergencyPrices");
    expect(d).to.have.property("branchOpen");
    expect(d).to.have.property("evaluatedAt");
  });
}

docs {
  Whether the active branch's orders are emergency-priced **right now**
  (Registration Settings → Emergency Pricing). Create Order uses it to show and
  price lab tests at their Emergency Price, and sends the state it priced with
  as `emergencyPricing` on `POST/PATCH /orders`.

  Login-only (no settings permission needed — order creators call it); exposes
  only booleans. Tenant + branch come from the JWT/active profile. A caller
  with no active branch (business tier) always gets `active: false`.

  Rule: `active = OverrideEmergencyPrices || (ApplyInNonOperatingHours &&
  branch closed now)`.
  - "Closed" = outside the branch's ACTIVE Schedule shifts, else outside its
    `operationalDays` + `openingTime`/`closingTime` — evaluated in the branch
    `timezone`, falling back to the tenant timezone (default Asia/Kolkata).
  - A branch with no operating hours configured is never closed here.

  Response `data`:
  - `active` — lab tests bill at Emergency Price now.
  - `reason` — `OVERRIDE` | `NON_OPERATING_HOURS` | `null` (Override wins when
    both apply).
  - `applyInNonOperatingHours` / `overrideEmergencyPrices` — the raw toggles.
  - `branchOpen` — `true`/`false` when the non-operating-hours toggle is on and
    the branch has hours configured; otherwise `null`.
  - `evaluatedAt` — ISO instant of the decision.
}
